==Scottish Gaelic==

===Etymology===
From the dative-locative singular of {{der|gd|sga|benn|t=peak, point, pinnacle}},<ref>{{R:DIL|5654|head=benn}}</ref> from {{der|gd|cel-pro|*bandā|t=peak, top}}. The development of this case form to a noun in its own right may be due to the substrate influence of the cognate {{der|gd|xpi|-}}/{{der|gd|cel-bry-pro|*bann}}, or the non-cognate {{m|cel-bry-pro|*penn}}. {{doublet|gd|beann}}.<ref>{{R:cel-bry:James:2020}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gd|/b̥ẽĩɲ/|[b̥ẽ̠ĩɲ]|ref={{R:Mac Gill-Fhinnein:1966}} !!! {{R:gd:Borgstrom1937}}|ref2={{R:gd:Oftedal}}}}
* {{IPA|gd|/b̥ɤ̃ĩɲ/|ref={{R:gd:Borgstrom1941|page=11}}|a=Skye}}
* {{IPA|gd|/b̥ĩːɲ/|ref={{R:gd:Wentworth:2003}}|a=Wester Ross}} {{q|as if spelled {{m|gd|binn}}}}

